les of an ideal HQNP look, name specific people as definitions of it, and compare it against other labels [3][4][5]. Another thread debates whether the category exists at all [6].","How it helps someone's own looks is indirect: the label gives members a shared description of a widely appealing look, and discussions around it compare traits such as skin, hair and grooming. Its meaning is set by usage, with no published definition."],"infobox":[["Type","Community slang / classification label"],["Stands for","High quality normie phenotype"],["Used on","looksmax.org"],["Contrasted with","Other phenotype labels, e.g. in 'hqnp vs hqp' threads"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["The label combines a quality grade (high quality) with a phenotype type (normie, meaning mainstream) [1][2]. Posters apply it to photos of women and to online personalities, and sometimes to personality or lifestyle traits, as in a thread claiming women who own cats are very HQNP [7]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"In looksmaxxing culture","paras":["Threads include rating requests, 'does she look HQNP' questions, praise threads and debates about whether HQNP women are rare, plentiful or mythical [1][3][4][6]. Contributors disagree about boundaries. Some threads contrast it with posts they consider heavily styled or cosmetic."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"On looksmax.org, HQNP is used both as a descriptive label and as a topic of argument about whether the type is attainable or common [1][6].","claims":[{"claim":"HQNP is an identifiable female look","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"HQNP women are rare or do not exist","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"HQNP Stacy n Betabuxxer Husband","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/hqnp-stacy-n-betabuxxer-husband.1771324/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2025,"type":"forum"},{"title":"does she look hqnp","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/does-she-look-hqnp.64581